{"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/optiviewadssdk.OptiViewAdsSDK\/documentation\/OptiViewAdsSDK\/OptiViewAdsConfig\/pdtGraceSeconds","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"pdtGraceSeconds","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"}],"platforms":["iOS","iPadOS","Mac Catalyst"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A session is normally started before the content player has loaded its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"source, so the scheduler’s first ticks see no PDT even on a stream that does"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"carry it. Those ticks make no scheduling decision, rather than matching breaks"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"against the system clock — which runs ahead of the live playhead by the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stream’s latency and would fire a break early (PLAYG-360)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"backstop, not a fixed delay","type":"text"}]},{"text":". The SDK stops waiting at whichever","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"comes first: content has been playing for ~1s and still exposes no PDT (direct","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"evidence about the stream — ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DA-PDT-MISSING"},{"text":" is emitted once and the clock","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"takes over immediately, so a join-in-progress break is not delayed below the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tune-in minimum), or this window elapses (the backstop for a player that never","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"starts).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Set "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0"},{"type":"text","text":" to fall back to the system clock immediately. Has no effect on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pts"},{"type":"text","text":"-timebase manifests. Mirrors the web "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pdtGraceSeconds"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/optiviewadssdk.OptiViewAdsSDK\/documentation\/OptiViewAdsSDK","doc:\/\/optiviewadssdk.OptiViewAdsSDK\/documentation\/OptiViewAdsSDK\/OptiViewAdsConfig"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How long, in seconds, to wait for the stream’s "},{"code":"EXT-X-PROGRAM-DATE-TIME","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"wallclock","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"-timebase session before concluding the stream carries none."}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"OptiViewAdsSDK"}],"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"pdtGraceSeconds","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Property","symbolKind":"property","externalID":"s:14OptiViewAdsSDK0abC6ConfigV15pdtGraceSecondsSdvp","title":"pdtGraceSeconds"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/optiviewadssdk\/optiviewadsconfig\/pdtgraceseconds"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://optiviewadssdk.OptiViewAdsSDK/documentation/OptiViewAdsSDK/OptiViewAdsConfig/pdtGraceSeconds":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/optiviewadssdk\/optiviewadsconfig\/pdtgraceseconds","type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/optiviewadssdk.OptiViewAdsSDK\/documentation\/OptiViewAdsSDK\/OptiViewAdsConfig\/pdtGraceSeco